@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-10-15

Feature: Project Init
  "Writes the short project .mason (site URL + build folder) for a new site, detecting the build folder when one exists."

  Provides:
    - setup.InitProject @source("symbol:InitProject")
    - setup.InitInput @source("symbol:InitInput")
    - setup.DetectBuildDir @source("symbol:DetectBuildDir")

  Consumes:
    - config.Load
    - config.NewSite

  Invariants:
    - InitProject MUST refuse to overwrite an existing .mason file
    - The written file MUST load through config.Load; on failure nothing MUST be left behind
    - InitProject MUST write only site, build, and (when given) server — never derived values like the server path
    - DetectBuildDir MUST return the first existing folder among dist, public, build, _site, out, or "" when none exists

  OutOfScope:
    - Provisioning the site on the server (cli init offers it; setup.ProvisionScript renders it)
    - Machine onboarding (setup.Run)

  Scenario (happy-path): Scaffold new project
    Given a directory with a dist/ folder and the URL https://blog.example.com
    When InitProject runs with the detected build folder
    Then .mason contains site: https://blog.example.com and build: dist

  Scenario (negative): Existing config
    Given .mason already exists
    When InitProject runs
    Then it returns an error without overwriting the file

  Scenario (negative): Invalid URL
    Given the URL https://example.com/blog
    When InitProject runs
    Then it fails explaining sites are served from the root of their host and writes nothing
